Cross-compiling NetHack 3.6.7 for m68k-AmigaOS
===============================================

Prerequisites
-------------

1. m68k-amigaos GCC toolchain
   Provides the cross-compiler, assembler, linker, and AmigaOS system headers.
   Expected at: /opt/amiga/bin/m68k-amigaos-gcc (and friends)

   The toolchain is available from:
     https://github.com/bebbo/amiga-gcc

   Tested with GCC 6.5.0b (bebbo fork).  The toolchain must include:
     - m68k-amigaos-gcc   (compiler)
     - m68k-amigaos-as    (assembler)
     - m68k-amigaos-ld    (linker, invoked via gcc -lamiga)
     - m68k-amigaos-ar    (archiver, for library inspection)
     - m68k-amigaos-nm    (symbol tool, for diagnostics)
     - libnix             (default C library, bundled with toolchain)
     - libamiga           (-lamiga, AmigaOS stubs, bundled with toolchain)

2. m68k-linux-gnu GCC toolchain
   Used to compile makedefs, lev_comp, and dgn_comp as static m68k Linux
   ELF binaries.  These are then run under qemu-m68k so their output is
   natively 32-bit big-endian — no post-processing or endian-conversion
   hacks are needed.

   On Debian/Ubuntu:
     apt install gcc-m68k-linux-gnu

3. QEMU user-mode emulation for m68k
   Runs the m68k-linux-gnu static binaries built in step 2.

   On Debian/Ubuntu:
     apt install qemu-user

   The binary must be available as: qemu-m68k

4. Native host GCC (gcc)
   Used to compile the dlb tool (the data archive packer).
   Any recent version on the build host is sufficient.

5. GNU make
   Used to drive the entire build.  Any version >= 3.81.

6. flex and bison
   Used to regenerate the level and dungeon compiler parsers if the
   grammar source files (.l, .y) are modified.  Pre-generated C sources
   are already present in util/, so flex and bison are only required if
   you need to change lev_comp or dgn_comp grammars.

   On Debian/Ubuntu:
     apt install flex bison


Build output
------------

All output lands under build-amiga/:

  build-amiga/NetHack/NetHack     AmigaOS m68k HUNK binary
  build-amiga/NetHack/nhdat       DLB archive (levels, text, options, etc.)
  build-amiga/NetHack/nhsdat      DLB archive (sounds)
  build-amiga/NetHack/*.font/     Amiga bitmap fonts
  build-amiga/NetHack/license     License file (read outside the archive)
  build-amiga/NetHack/symbols     Symbol definitions (read outside archive)


Building
--------

  # Full build: binary + all data files
  make -f sys/amiga/Makefile.cross

  # Binary only (no data)
  make -f sys/amiga/Makefile.cross obj link

  # Data files only
  make -f sys/amiga/Makefile.cross data

  # Remove object files (keeps data and binary)
  make -f sys/amiga/Makefile.cross clean

  # Remove everything built
  make -f sys/amiga/Makefile.cross spotless
